lists.description:
Shared block lists, each a file of Mastodon's domain block CSV
pinned by its SHA-256, whose domains are blocked beside `block`'s;
`[federation]`'s where unset.

proxy.description:
The proxy herald's own requests go through: "environment", the
host's `HTTPS_PROXY` and `NO_PROXY` where it honours them; "none";
or a proxy's http or https URL. "environment" where absent.

replies.description:
Whether answers to `latest` and `changelog` are posted to the room;
Matrix has no answer seen by one member alone, so `ephemeral` answers
in a thread under the command.

alerts.description:
Which security alerts are announced where the signals take
"alert": what raised them, what they did and how severe they are;
every tool's raised and reopened alerts where absent.

transport.description:
How an owner's members are polled; "auto" where absent. GitHub
offers auto, graphql, rest and events; GitLab auto, graphql and rest;
Forgejo auto, rest and feed.

